# OnKith local settings.
#
# The canonical location is the REPOSITORY ROOT:
#
#   cp FullPipeline_V6/.env.example .env      # from the repository root
#
# One ignored `.env` beside the repository serves the live pipeline and all
# three benchmarks, so a key never has to be copied into this directory. A
# `.env` here is still read, and wins, but nothing requires one.
#
# `.env` is excluded by .gitignore and by scripts/build_release_zip.py. Never
# put a real key in this file, in source, in a ZIP, or in a chat window.
#
# Values are read with os.environ.setdefault, so the order of precedence is:
#
#   process environment  ->  FullPipeline_V6/.env  ->  <repo root>/.env  ->  defaults
#
# A variable already exported in the shell always wins, which is how the no-key
# mode is tested without renaming or deleting anybody's file. Only the keys
# listed below are read at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language model. Optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without it, Whisper, masking, SQLite, local commands, the terminal UI, the
# localhost UI and local TTS all still start. A question then clears the privacy
# gate, the screen shows the masked text that *would* have been sent, and no
# network request is made. That degraded mode is a supported way to run the
# demo, not a failure.
#
# Free keys: https://console.groq.com/keys  (Groq, not xAI Grok)
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Both defaults are production models in Groq's free tier. Check a name against
# the live catalogue before changing it - a withdrawn name returns HTTP 404 and
# reads on screen as the device being offline:
#
#   curl -sH "Authorization: Bearer $GROQ_API_KEY" \
#        -H "User-Agent: Onkith/1.0" \
#        https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/models
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
GROQ_FALLBACK_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local text to speech. Optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset, the engine picks the first backend actually installed, in this order:
# kokoro, piper, sapi (Windows System.Speech), espeak-ng, say. Set it to pin one
# explicitly, or to `none` to run silent. TTS speaks the locally restored answer,
# never the masked one, and a synthesis failure never breaks the pipeline.
ONKITH_TTS=

# Piper needs a local voice model. models/piper/ ships only the .json companion;
# fetch the matching .onnx with scripts/download_large_models.py, then point at
# it here with an absolute path.
ONKITH_PIPER_MODEL=

# Kokoro needs the kokoro-onnx build plus its own model and voice pack. Not
# installed by default: the graph is ~310 MB, which a 4 GB Pi cannot hold beside
# the recognizer and the classifier.
ONKITH_KOKORO_MODEL=
ONKITH_KOKORO_VOICES=
ONKITH_KOKORO_VOICE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local surfaces. Optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser used for the localhost assistant UI. Empty means chromium, then
# chromium-browser, then google-chrome, then the system default. `--headless`
# keeps the LLM and TTS lanes without opening any window at all.
ONKITH_UI_BROWSER=

# Local music search. Optional; the music route is inert without it.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
YOUTUBE_REGION=
